# Repository safety

- Work only inside the current repository mounted at `${PROJECT_DIR}` (path parity with the host).
- Do not read or modify host paths outside `${PROJECT_DIR}`.
- Do not try to bypass container limits or security controls.
- Do not read secrets, private keys, or credential files.
- Do not modify `.env` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not run destructive commands unless the user clearly requests them.
- Do not run `docker system prune` or similar cleanup that deletes unrelated resources.
- Do not delete host data under `CIND_DATA` (`~/.config/cind`) unless the user explicitly requests `make clean-data` / `make clean-volumes`.
- Do not start containers with `--privileged`.
- Do not mount `/`, `/home`, `/etc`, or other sensitive host paths into containers (except the intentional `CIND_DATA` binds under `~/.config/cind`).
- Treat `/var/run/docker.sock` as privileged host access; enable it only with `*-docker` Make targets.
